Subject: [lojban] Military language

 

Does language figure into warfare? Do common ambiguities in English result
directly in death, or loss? We have "military time", and various military
linguistic traditions "SIR, yes, SIR".
 
The SW hypothesis asks if language influences thought. Does it influence who
lives and who dies?
 
This is both of historic importance and also of coming relevance, especially
when combined with transhumanistic technologies.
 
ii ru'e

           
